    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106037" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τυρσηνός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, 
			Ion.
		 for 
			Att.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τυρρηνός;</span>
		
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τυρσᾱνός</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>P.</u>
			1.72
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>SIG</u>
			14
		</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">vi/v B. C.</span>), also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τυρρᾱνός</span></b>  (v. infr.):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Tyrrhenian, Etruscan,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Hom.
				7.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				1016
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				1359
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ Δὶ Τυράν᾽ ἀπὸ Κύμας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					35
				</span></i>
			 (Olympia, V B.C.), cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τυρρανοί</span> ib. <i><span class="en">
				24
			</span></i> (Delph.):— the people were <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τυρσηνοί</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τυρρηνοί</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.57
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τ. Πελασγοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					270
				</span></i>
			 (anap.):—Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τυρσηνικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, σάλπιγξ, κώδων,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				567
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				17
			</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κηρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.3
				</span></i>
			: also fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τυρσηνίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, Σκύλλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					1342
				</span></i>
			.</div>
